hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"18000","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Ibn Jurayj, he said, Ismail ibn Kathir narrated to me, from Asim ibn Laqit, from his father, the delegate of Banu al-Muntafiq, and Abd al-Razzaq said, al-Muntafiq, that he and a companion of his set out to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) but did not find him. Aishah fed them dates and porridge. Soon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came walking briskly, swaying. So he said, Did you feed them. We said, Yes. I said, O Messenger of Allah, I ask you about prayer. He said, Perfect ablution, run water between the fingers, and when you sniff water go deep, unless you are fasting. I said, O Messenger of Allah, I have a wife, and he mentioned her foul tongue. He said, Divorce her. I said, She has companionship and a child. He said, Command her, or say to her, if good is in her she will do it. And do not beat your wife as you beat your bondwoman. While he was thus, the shepherd drove the sheep into the pen with a kid in his hand. So he said, Did it give birth. He said, Yes. He said, What. He said, A young goat. He said, Slaughter a sheep in its place. Then he turned to me and said, Do not think, and he did not say, let him not think, that we slaughtered it for your sake. We have a hundred sheep and dislike increase upon them. When the shepherd delivers a young goat we order him to slaughter a sheep in its place."
